---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Email from '../components/Email.astro';
---

<Base title="About — Matka Ceramics">
  <section class="mk-page">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      Matka Ceramics is Sumedha Mehta, working out of Brooklyn. Everything here is
      thrown, glazed and photographed by hand, and every piece is one of a kind —
      glaze tests rarely repeat, so when something is gone it stays on the site
      marked sold rather than disappearing.
    </p>

    <p>
      The forms come from Indian domestic pottery: the matka, the khullad, the
      kolam drawn at a threshold. They are made to be used daily, not kept for good.
    </p>

    <h2>Care</h2>
    <p>
      Dishwasher and microwave safe unless a piece says otherwise. Unglazed
      terracotta will darken with use — that is the clay doing what clay does, not
      a fault. Avoid sudden temperature changes; don't take a piece from the fridge
      to a hot oven.
    </p>

    <h2>Shipping and returns</h2>
    <p>
      Orders ship from Brooklyn within 3–5 business days, to the US and Canada.
      You'll get a tracking number by email when the label is printed.
    </p>
    <p>
      If something arrives broken, email me with a photo and I'll refund it. Because
      pieces are one of a kind I usually can't send a replacement.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Email <Email />, or find me on
      <a href="https://www.instagram.com/matkaceramics/" rel="me">Instagram</a>,
      where new work is announced first.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
